  "narrative": {
    "intro": "Oracle Health Government Services has federal contract obligations totaling $1.3B in FY2026 to date. Oracle Health Government Services has 28 awards this fiscal year and an average award size of $45.9M. Oracle Health Government Services obligations are up 27.6% year over year. Oracle Health Government Services obligations have varied in recent years: FY21 was $971M, FY22 was $2B, FY23 was $825M, FY24 was $893M, FY25 was $1B, and FY26 is $1.3B. Oracle Health Government Services primary market this fiscal year is Computer Systems Design Services at $1.3B. Oracle Health Government Services also has smaller activity in Computer Facilities Management Services at $3.6M and Used Household and Office Goods Moving at $110K. Oracle Health Government Services shows a clear concentration of federal spending in one agency and one NAICS market for FY2026 to date, with other agencies and markets showing zero or minimal obligations.",
